# Story 80: Spawning a Humanoid (45s)
# Hook: Inline prompt or a skill file with a contacts block -- either way, it's one command.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-080-spawning-a-humanoid.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Inline prompt or a skill file with a contacts block -- either way, it's one command.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Launch rysh. The quickest way is an inline system prompt.

[00:08.0 --> 00:18.0]
For real channels, write a skill file. It looks like an agent skill file but adds a contacts section -- here, a Slack block with tokens and channels.

[00:18.0 --> 00:28.0]
Cat it: name, description, model, then the contacts block. The ENV_VAR syntax pulls secrets from the environment at parse time.

[00:28.0 --> 00:38.0]
Double-Escape into rysh mode and spawn from the file with ##humanoid spawn. Rysh wires up every channel in the contacts block.

[00:38.0 --> 00:45.0]
##humanoid list shows it running, with its Slack channel attached.

